<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Nedao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">454</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Nedao was fought in 454 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a> between the sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a> and a coalition of their former subject peoples led by the Gepid king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardaric">Ardaric</a>. The rebels won, and Attila's eldest son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ellac">Ellac</a> was killed. The battle ended Hun domination in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and let the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gepids">Gepids</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrogoths">Ostrogoths</a> and others form their own kingdoms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-nedao.jpg" alt="Battle of Nedao" width="320" height="262" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ikonact · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pannonian_Basin_geographic_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
